<title>USA: U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Census Bureau reports</p>
<p>factory consumption of domestic and foreign cotton (bales):</p>
<p>    Feb 97-A   Jan 97-B    Feb 96   Cum 1997   Cum 1996</p>
<p>     823,084    809,802   786,813  1,632,886  1,525,711</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE CONSUMPTION OF ALL COTTON (bales):</p>
<p>    Feb 97-Y   Jan 97-X   Feb 96</p>
<p>	40,128     40,769   39,341</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE SPINDLE HOURS OPERATED:</p>
<p>    Feb 97-X  Jan 96-Y   Feb 96</p>
<p>	   142	 143	153</p>
<p>A-4 weeks. B-4 weeks. X-Based on 20 days. Y-20 days.</p>
</text>
